    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Points system** (replacing the old direct-level rules) in `OwnerMembershipLevelPolicy.java`:\n- Start at 0; `+2` email present, `+1` `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` household of 3+, `+3` tenure > 365 days.\n- `membershipPoints` \u2192 `membershipLevel`: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n- Both `membershipPoints(owner)` and `membershipLevel(owner)` are exposed and returned.\n\n**Four files touched, each edit kept small and cohesive:**\n1. `OwnerMembershipLevelPolicy.java` \u2014 the two point-scoring methods plus a small private `householdSize` helper. It now injects `ClinicService` via the same static-component pattern already used by `OwnerBulkSignupPolicy`, so household size (owners sharing `householdId`) is countable without touching the mapper/controller/service or growing any large class.\n2. `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line for `membershipPoints`.\n3. `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema field and updated `membershipLevel` (now 1\u20134) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries both.\n\nThe scoring lives in one tiny, low-complexity policy class rather than being spread into the mapper or controller, keeping WMC_other and the touched-file count low. The acceptance test (email + no namesake, single household, zero tenure \u2192 3 points, level 2) passes.",
