    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`, traced through the actual code.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Request binding & Bean Validation (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`)\n\nApplied to the incoming JSON before the controller body runs:\n\n1. **firstName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/apostrophe/hyphen)\n2. **lastName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n3. **address** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")` (non-blank)\n4. **city** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")` (non-blank)\n5. **telephone** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern` requiring **exactly 10 digits**\n6. **email** \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n7. **postcode** \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` (optional)\n8. **registrationDate / birthDate** \u2014 `@Valid` LocalDate (optional)\n\nAuthorization gate: `@PreAuthorize` requires role **OWNER_ADMIN**.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Mapper normalization & mutation (`ownerMapper.toOwner`)\n\n9. **address** normalized: trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`\n10. **telephone** converted to E.164 (strip separators, assume `+61`, drop leading `0`); if 8\u201315 digits, `OwnerTelephoneLengthPolicy` validates national length (**400** if `+61`\u22609 or `+1`\u226010 national digits)\n11. **email** lowercased\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Controller policy pipeline (in exact call order)\n\n12. **RegistrationDatePolicy** \u2014 reject future date (400); default to today if absent; roll weekend \u2192 Monday. *(mutates registrationDate)*\n13. **DailyLimitPolicy** \u2014 `findAllOwners()`; reject if \u2265100 owners share that registration date (**429**)\n14. **CityCapacityPolicy** \u2014 `findAllOwners()`; reject if city already has \u226550 owners (**409**)\n15. **PostcodePolicy** \u2014 for Sydney/Melbourne/Brisbane, enforce state postcode range (throws `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2014 note: **surfaces as 500**, not 400, because no matching handler exists)\n16. **DisposableEmailPolicy** \u2014 reject mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail domains (**400**)\n17. **HouseholdPolicy** \u2014 compute `householdId` = SHA-256(lastName|postcode); `findAllOwners()`; reject duplicate (lastName, postcode) unless `sharesHousehold == true` (**409**). *(mutates householdId)*\n18. **NamesakePolicy** \u2014 set `namesakeCount` = count of existing same first+last name. *(mutates namesakeCount)*\n19. **CustomerCodePolicy** \u2014 set `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`. *(mutates customerCode)*\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Persist (`clinicService.saveOwner` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save`)\n\n20. Runs inside the service-layer **`@Transactional`** boundary (controller itself is not transactional)\n21. Entity-level Bean Validation on `Owner`/`Person` at persist (`@NotEmpty` names/address/city; telephone `@Pattern` E.164 `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`)\n22. **`@PrePersist`** callback `defaultRegistrationDate()` \u2014 sets registrationDate to today if still null (already set in step 12)\n23. No cascade (pets is null on create); no `@EntityListeners`, no `@CreatedDate`/auditing, no events, no email\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 After save\n\n24. **AuditPolicy.auditCreate** \u2014 emits an SLF4J `AUDIT` **log line** (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel); no DB write\n25. **`toOwnerDto`** builds the 201 body, invoking read-only derivation policies (telephone display, check digit, membership, locality, age band, etc. \u2014 no persistence side-effects)\n26. Sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, returns **201 Created**\n\n## Things notably *absent* (despite scaffolding existing)\n- **No uniqueness check on telephone, email, or identity** \u2014 the `DuplicateTelephone/Email/Identity` exception handlers are registered, but the methods that throw them are never called on this path.\n- No password/encoding (Owner has no password).\n- The `CallMonitoringAspect` does **not** intercept the save (Spring Data repo isn't `@Repository`-annotated).\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: the `InvalidPostcodeException` (step 15) is annotated `@ResponseStatus(BAD_REQUEST)` but lacks a dedicated `@ExceptionHandler`, so the catch-all `Exception \u2192 500` handler wins \u2014 an out-of-range postcode is reported as **500**, unlike every other policy rejection."
